            <ArticleTitle>Preterm torsion of a gravid uterus didelphys horn of a twin pregnancy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1186-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Simultaneous pregnancy in each horn of a uterus didelphys is a rare and complex clinical situation.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE" NlmCategory="METHODS">Torsion of one horn of a gravid didelphic uterus during a twin pregnancy was diagnosed during cesarean delivery after erroneous diagnosis of abruptio placentae.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Localization of the placenta in a pregnancy complicated by uterine didelphys may improve the ability to diagnose hemiuterus torsion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
